  "description": "#6527 — READ-command differential over `resolve_page_title`, the single-title lookup the New page dialog, the welcome tour, the Templates view and the date picker ask instead of listing every page of the space. It answers as `create_page_in_space` resolves a title (`SpacePageNames`, #6278): the live page titled under `name_key` (trim, Unicode case, NFC), the smallest id first, with its title as written; else the trimmed title. Titles only: S2's alias `plans` answers no page. A blank title takes the first free `Untitled N` among the titles: S4 `Untitled` and S5 `untitled 2` (another case) are taken, S6 `Untitled 4` is past the first gap, so the answer is `Untitled 3`. The one op trashes S3, whose title then answers no page. S7 and S8 hold one title in two cases, as a vault from before titles were unique per space may: the smaller id answers, the page a create opens. Every step answers one row, so none is declared empty.",
